# Demo scenario of the PharmacyDelivery API (VS / Rider HTTP client, VS Code REST Client).
# Stand: docker compose up -d --build  (or dotnet run --project src/PharmacyDelivery.Api). Data template: demo.
# Run the requests top to bottom: named requests (# @name) pass ids and tokens to the next ones.
# Password of every demo account: Demo-Password-2026!  — test stand only.

@host = http://localhost:5080
@api = {{host}}/api/v1
@password = Demo-Password-2026!

### Health (environment, version, dependencies)
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### 1. Catalog (anonymous)
# @name products
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?search=acetaminophen&page=1&pageSize=5

### 2. Customer login
# @name customer
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "emily.johnson@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 3. Put the first found product into the cart (quantity 1–10)
PUT {{api}}/cart/items/{{products.response.body.items[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 2 }

### 4. Cart
GET {{api}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5. Checkout — response: the pharmacy that will deliver and the ETA
# Idempotency-Key: repeat the request with the same key → 200 with the same order instead of a second order.
# @name checkout
POST {{api}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-{{$timestamp}}

{
  "address": { "street": "11 E 36th St", "city": "New York", "postalCode": "10016", "latitude": 40.7493, "longitude": -73.9822 }
}

### 6. Start the payment (fake PSP)
# @name payment
POST {{api}}/orders/{{checkout.response.body.orderId}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. PSP decides — sends the HMAC-signed webhook to /api/v1/webhooks/psp (Development/Test only)
POST {{api}}/dev/psp/payments/{{payment.response.body.providerPaymentId}}/complete?result=succeeded

### 8. Order: status (paid → assignedToPharmacy after the OrderPaid consumer), pharmacy, ETA, history
GET {{api}}/orders/{{checkout.response.body.orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9. Pharmacist of the selected pharmacy
# The account is pharmacist.<pharmacy code>@pharmacy-delivery.local — the code is in the checkout response (pharmacy.code), e.g. NYC-MID.
# @name pharmacist
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "pharmacist.nyc-mid@pharmacy-delivery.local", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 10. Pharmacy queue
GET {{api}}/pharmacy/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmacist.response.body.accessToken}}

### 11. Accept (within Pharmacy:AcceptanceTimeoutMinutes, otherwise the order moves to the next pharmacy)
POST {{api}}/pharmacy/orders/{{checkout.response.body.orderId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmacist.response.body.accessToken}}

### 12. Packed → stock committed, OrderReadyForPickup → dispatch assigns the nearest free courier
POST {{api}}/pharmacy/orders/{{checkout.response.body.orderId}}/ready
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmacist.response.body.accessToken}}

### 13. Tracking: courier position is visible only while the order is inDelivery (the simulator drives automatically)
GET {{api}}/orders/{{checkout.response.body.orderId}}/tracking
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.accessToken}}

### --- Courier side (what the simulator does) ---

### Courier login
# @name courier
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "courier1@pharmacy-delivery.local", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Current delivery of the courier
# @name delivery
GET {{api}}/courier/deliveries/current
Authorization: Bearer {{courier.response.body.accessToken}}

### Picked up at the pharmacy → order inDelivery
POST {{api}}/courier/deliveries/{{delivery.response.body.deliveryId}}/pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{courier.response.body.accessToken}}

### GPS batch (max Tracking:MaxBatchSize points; implausible jumps are dropped)
POST {{api}}/courier/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{courier.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "points": [ { "latitude": 40.7490, "longitude": -73.9880, "recordedAt": "{{$datetime iso8601}}", "speedKmh": 25 } ] }

### Delivered
POST {{api}}/courier/deliveries/{{delivery.response.body.deliveryId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{courier.response.body.accessToken}}

### --- Session management ---

### Refresh (rotation: the old refresh token stops working; reusing it revokes the whole session)
POST {{api}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{customer.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### Active sessions
GET {{api}}/auth/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.accessToken}}

### Logout — the access token is revoked immediately (next call → 401)
POST {{api}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.accessToken}}

### --- Admin ---

### Admin login
# @name admin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@pharmacy-delivery.local", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Audit log of an order (old → new values)
GET {{api}}/admin/audit?entityType=Order&entityId={{checkout.response.body.orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Reset all data to the demo template (Development/Test only)
POST {{api}}/admin/maintenance/seed/reset
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "profile": "demo" }
